## 📋 Prerequisites

- **Node.js 24** — the version in `.nvmrc` (`nvm use`).
{{#if (eq packageManager "pnpm")}}
- **pnpm** — the version in `package.json#packageManager`, activated with `corepack enable`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq packageManager "yarn")}}
- **Yarn** — the version in `package.json#packageManager`, activated with `corepack enable`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq packageManager "bun")}}
- **Bun** — the version in `package.json#packageManager`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq packageManager "npm")}}
- **npm 11.16 or newer** — it enforces the install-script allowlist in `package.json#allowScripts`.
{{/if}}
{{#if database}}
- **Docker** with Compose — runs the local {{#if (eq database.engine "postgres")}}PostgreSQL{{else}}MySQL{{/if}} database.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq auth "better-auth")}}
- **openssl** — the setup script generates the auth secret with it.
{{/if}}

## 🚀 Getting started

Fresh clone? The setup script creates `.env` from `.env.example`{{#if (eq auth "better-auth")}} (generating the auth secret){{/if}}, installs dependencies{{#if database}}, starts the database and applies the schema{{/if}}:

```bash
bash scripts/setup.sh          # interactive
bash scripts/setup.sh --yes    # non-interactive
```

Then start the dev server:

```bash
{{packageManager}} run dev
```

`src/env.ts` validates the environment at build and start; every variable it reads is listed in `.env.example`.

## 📜 Scripts

| Command | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `{{packageManager}} run setup` | Create `.env`, install dependencies{{#if database}} and prepare the database{{/if}} |
| `{{packageManager}} run dev` | Start the dev server |
| `{{packageManager}} run build` | Build for production |
| `{{packageManager}} run start` | Start the production server |
| `{{packageManager}} run check` | Type-check, lint, format-check and unused-code check |
| `{{packageManager}} run fix` | Fix lint findings and format |
| `{{packageManager}} run typecheck` | Type-check |
| `{{packageManager}} run lint` | Run ESLint (`lint:fix` to fix) |
| `{{packageManager}} run format` | Format with Prettier (`format:check` to check) |
| `{{packageManager}} run knip` | Report unused files, exports and dependencies |
| `{{packageManager}} run test` | Run the tests (`test:watch` to watch) |
{{#if (eq database.orm "drizzle")}}
| `{{packageManager}} run db:generate` | Generate a migration from the schema |
| `{{packageManager}} run db:migrate` | Apply pending migrations |
| `{{packageManager}} run db:push` | Push the schema without a migration (local throwaway databases only) |
| `{{packageManager}} run db:studio` | Open Drizzle Studio |
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq database.orm "prisma")}}
| `{{packageManager}} run db:generate` | Generate the Prisma client |
| `{{packageManager}} run db:migrate` | Create and apply a migration from the schema |
| `{{packageManager}} run db:push` | Push the schema without a migration (local throwaway databases only) |
| `{{packageManager}} run db:studio` | Open Prisma Studio |
{{/if}}

## 🗂️ Project structure

```text
src/
  app/                  routing only: pages, layouts, route handlers
  features/<domain>/    one vertical slice per domain: components, server code, schemas
  components/           domain-free building blocks{{#if shadcn}}; components/ui/ holds the shadcn primitives{{/if}}
  lib/                  infrastructure{{#if database}}: database client and schema{{/if}}{{#if (eq auth "better-auth")}}, auth{{/if}}{{#if (eq email "resend")}}, email{{/if}}{{#if (or api (eq auth "better-auth") (and production database))}}, logger{{/if}}{{#if (or api (eq auth "better-auth"))}}, the error model{{/if}}
{{#if api}}
  {{api.type}}/                 the API layer: procedure builders, router, clients
{{/if}}
  env.ts                the only place that reads process.env
```

Features import only from themselves, `lib/`, `components/` and the project infrastructure; ESLint enforces these boundaries.
{{#if production}}

